    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-080 — list-style-type and ::marker rendering.** Fixes the 1,559 `<li>` elements on Wikipedia's HTML article that were rendering as plain indented text with no bullet.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Data model** (`layout_box.hpp`):\n- `Display::ListItem` enum value\n- `LayoutBox::list_style_type` field (empty = not a list item)\n\n**Cascade** (`cascade.cpp` + `stylesheet.cpp`):\n- `\"list-style-type\"` in `is_inherited` (ul/ol → li per CSS)\n- `\"list-style-type\"` in `supported_properties` whitelist\n\n**UA stylesheet** (`ua_stylesheet.cpp`):\n```css\nul { list-style-type: disc }\nol { list-style-type: decimal }\nli { display: list-item }\n```\n\n**Layout** (`layout.cpp`):\n- `display_of` handles `list-item`\n- Captures `list_style_type` on boxes whose own display is `list-item`\n\n**Paint** (`paint.cpp`):\n- `disc` (filled circle, r=3), `circle` (stroke), `square` (fill)\n- `(box.x-20, box.y+10)` — inside the 40px `padding-left` from UA\n- Color `#202122` (Wikipedia body text)\n\n## Verified (Wikipedia)\n\n| Location | Result |\n|---|---|\n| See also section | ✅ Bullets visible |\n| Navboxes (Web browsers, W3C) | ✅ Bullets visible |\n| Hamburger menu | ✅ Bullets visible |\n| TOC left sidebar | ✅ No bullets (correct — `list-style-type: none` in cascade) |\n| Sidebar categories | Depends on element; content lists show bullets |\n\n## Tests\n\n- **5 new** ADR-080 tests + 1 UA rules-count update\n- Suite: **707 → 716 cases**, **2673 → 2702 assertions**, all green\n\n## Deferred\n\n- **Ordered list ordinal markers** (`1.`, `2.`, `3.`) — needs counter state per-list\n- **Roman, alphabetic, custom counter styles** — `@counter-style` support\n- **`::marker` pseudo-element styling** — Wikipedia uses this rarely\n- **`list-style-position: inside`** — rare on Wikipedia\n- **Marker color inheritance** — drawn in `#202122` regardless of `li` color\n\n## What this is\n\nFirst ADR from the **feature inventory** (this session's audit of `merged.css` vs HoneyBee source). Not a bug fix — a **measured feature gap** with a specific use count (24 `list-style-type`, 1,559 `<li>` elements affected). Follows the pattern of ADR-077/078: focused scope, tested, verified visually.\n\n## Verification category\n\n**Unit-tested + production-visible.**\n\nRefs #290\n",
